.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt BLESS 8
.Os Minkar
.Sh NAME
.Nm bless
.Nd set a volume's boot information and the boot device
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl -info Op Ar mountpoint
.Nm
.Fl -folder Ar directory
.Op Fl -file Ar file
.Op Fl -setBoot
.Nm
.Fl -unbless Ar directory
.Nm
.Fl -mount Ar mountpoint | Fl -device Ar device
.Fl -setBoot
.Op Fl -bootefi Ar file
.Nm
.Fl -getBoot
.Sh DESCRIPTION
An HFS+ volume keeps its boot information in its header: the blessed
system folder, the blessed booter file, the open-folder list, an alternate
OS's folder, an unused word and the OS X blessed folder (each a catalog
ID), and the volume's 64-bit ID.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl -info Op Ar mountpoint
Show the boot information of the volume holding
.Ar mountpoint
(the root volume by default), with the paths the IDs name.
.It Fl -folder Ar directory Op Fl -file Ar file
Bless the folder (as the system folder and the OS X blessed folder) and
the booter file, on their volume.
.It Fl -unbless Ar directory
Take the folder's blessing away, and its booter's.
.It Fl -getBoot
Print the device the firmware boots from: the one the
.Va efi-boot-device
NVRAM variable names, or, when it is not set, the volume the system started
from.
.It Fl -setBoot
Make the volume given
.Pf ( Fl -mount ,
.Fl -device
or
.Fl -folder )
start: Minkar's loader and kernel cache, as the EFI System Partition of the
running system's disk has them (or the loader
.Fl -bootefi
names), go into the EFI System Partition of the volume's disk, at the
firmware's default path, with a boot configuration naming the volume and
keeping the running system's other boot settings.
NVRAM variables can't be written on this system yet: the firmware starts
the disk by its default path.
.It Fl -bootefi Ar file
The loader
.Fl -setBoot
installs.
.El
.Pp
.Fl -verbose ,
.Fl -quiet ,
.Fl -nextonly ,
.Fl -legacy ,
and
.Fl -label
are accepted.
Blessing needs root.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on an error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nvram 8 ,
.Xr systemsetup 8
